 "about": {
  "text": "This year, we’re once again celebrating Halloween with a double feature. Thematically, this event is tied to the monthly program “Reclaiming Youth.” As a preview to the home-invasion thriller SEEDS (2024), we’re screening CLEARCUT (1991). Because even though this brutal folk-horror western—unlike SEEDS—has been around for a few years now and wasn’t made in an Indigenous context, this obscure cult film has certainly helped pave the way for such young voices. In both films, bloody revenge is set against the backdrop of stereotypical portrayals of Indigenous people as pacifists. …",
